class.description:
A goal states [i]what[/i] the agent wants, never [i]how[/i] to get it; finding the how is [GoapPlanner]'s job. Give an agent a handful of goals and it will pursue the highest priority one it can currently build a plan for. [codeblock] extends GoapGoal
func _init(): goal_name = &"stay_alive" desired_state = {&"is_safe": true}
func _get_priority(context): # Outranks everything else once wounded. return 100.0 if context.get_state(&"health", 100) < 30 else 1.0 [/codeblock] Goals that are already satisfied are skipped, so the agent falls through to the next one instead of idling. A low priority goal with an easily satisfied state, such as [code]{&"is_idle": true}[/code], makes a good fallback.
